insert into public.blog_posts select * from json_populate_recordset(null::public.blog_posts, E'[{"id":"3b1ccc7a-54df-4e64-b4bc-9a8258eae85c","slug":"world-cup-2026-knockouts-local-time","title":"How to follow the World Cup 2026 knockout rounds in your time zone","dek":"The bracket moves fast and kickoffs land at awkward hours. Here is how to keep every knockout match in your own local time — and never miss the start.","body_markdown":"The group stage is a marathon; the knockouts are a sprint. Once the World Cup reaches the round of 32, every match is win-or-go-home, the schedule tightens, and the fixtures you actually want can land in the middle of your night depending on where you are watching from.\\n\\n## Why the times are confusing\\n\\nMatches are published in the venue''s local time, then shifted again for broadcast. A kickoff listed as one time in a host city is a completely different time where you live, and the offset is exactly the part that trips people up. During the knockouts, with games stacked across a single weekend, that math gets old fast.\\n\\n## Keep it in your own time zone\\n\\nSilbo Sports converts every kickoff to the time zone on your device, so you see when a match actually starts where you are — no working out the offset, no missed games. Follow a nation and its next fixture sits in one schedule with the local time already sorted.\\n\\nYou can also:\\n\\n- Add any match to your phone or desktop calendar with one tap\\n- Subscribe once to a live feed that updates itself if a time moves\\n- Turn on a reminder so you get a nudge before kickoff\\n- Check the where-to-watch links for the broadcasters carrying the match in your region\\n\\n## As the bracket resolves\\n\\nKnockout fixtures start as placeholders — the winner of one group against a third-placed team from another — and resolve to real teams as the group stage finishes. Silbo follows the live schedule, so once the matchup is set, the names, times, and venue update in place. You follow the team; we keep the fixture current.\\n\\nWhether you are tracking one nation or the whole bracket, the goal is the same: spend less time doing timezone arithmetic and more time watching the football.","hero_image_url":null,"sport_key":"soccer","related_event_id":null,"seo_description":"Convert every World Cup 2026 knockout kickoff to your local time, add matches to your calendar, and get reminders with Silbo Sports.","author":"Silbo Sports","status":"published","published_at":"2026-06-29T22:29:33.357428+00:00","created_at":"2026-06-29T22:29:33.357428+00:00","updated_at":"2026-07-02T04:30:00.035216+00:00"}]'::json) on conflict do nothing;
